  "interpretation": [
    "The probe confirms that Trade does have economically meaningful strategic-winner states; current strategic-winner exit signals have much longer holding periods and stronger excess-return history than ordinary/unvalidated exits.",
    "However, ATR trailing stops on the extreme winners are not simply redundant profit-taking. Every deferred ATR signal in this counterfactual occurred with price below the short moving average, and median close-known 60-session relative strength was already negative.",
    "Deferring those ATR exits allowed larger winners to remain exposed through deteriorating trend state, then created more later sell/rebuy chains. The result was lower return, slightly deeper drawdown, lower Sharpe/Calmar, and more fills.",
    "Therefore the specific rule 'profit lock active => defer ATR trailing' is rejected. Phase 1 provides no evidence to weaken or bypass ATR trailing globally for winners.",
    "The useful retained finding is narrower: winner lifecycle is a real state dimension, but any future production use must preserve trend deterioration as authoritative rather than treating accumulated profit alone as a reason to hold longer."
  ],
